Room: //room hears each DevTools layout update.

Room docks DevTools in its own card (5.10, the user: DevTools' own Dock side
menu and close button rather than Room's strip). Chrome lets DevTools dock
only when the inspected Browser has a DevtoolsUIController; //room registers
one with no ContentsContainerView (a host-owned window has none), so Chrome
docks, and the front-end shows its Dock side menu and close button. Every
layout change then reaches DevtoolsUIController::UpdateDevtools (shown docked,
undocked, the front-end's split moved through SetInspectedPageBounds, the
window closing), which is non-virtual and lays out only Views containers.

The hook tells //room, which reads DevToolsWindow::GetInTabWebContents and
the resizing strategy and tells the host. Nothing else changes in Chrome.

Phase 5.10, 2026-11-01. //room: room/core/room_web_contents_tools.mm,
room/core/room_browser.mm.
